# evidence-cmd: cd plugins/webster && python3 scripts/doctype.py types > /tmp/webster-c3-types.txt; echo "types exit=$?"; sed -n '/^Audiences/,/^ISO/p' /tmp/webster-c3-types.txt; echo "lines naming command-line flags: $(grep -c 'command-line flags' /tmp/webster-c3-types.txt)"; rm -rf /tmp/webster-c3-flags && mkdir -p /tmp/webster-c3-flags/user/docs /tmp/webster-c3-flags/op/docs && printf '%s\n' '---' 'title: Guide' 'doc_type: how-to' 'audience: user' '---' '' '# Guide' '' 'Run it with `--verbose` and `-v`.' > /tmp/webster-c3-flags/user/docs/guide.md && sed 's/audience: user/audience: operator/' /tmp/webster-c3-flags/user/docs/guide.md > /tmp/webster-c3-flags/op/docs/guide.md && echo '--- user page ---' && python3 scripts/doctype.py check /tmp/webster-c3-flags/user/docs; echo "exit=$?"; echo '--- operator page ---'; python3 scripts/doctype.py check /tmp/webster-c3-flags/op/docs; echo "exit=$?"
# evidence-for: FR-012, FR-017
#
# D-041. The contract `doctype.py types` prints, next to the behaviour it describes.
# The user line now names command-line flags and any route path — the two classes
# FR-012 and FR-011 added while the printed list still said "internal symbols, routes,
# environment variables and architecture". Below it, the same flag on a user page is a
# wrong-lens defect and on an operator page is silent, which is the gate GI-003 and
# FR-017 ask for and the reason the operator line must not pick the flags up.
types exit=0
Audiences. The audience is a lens first and a reading grade second:
  user       grade 10  Uses the product. No development, sysadmin or DevOps background.
             assumes general computer literacy and a real reason to be here
             may not name internal symbols, any route path, command-line flags, environment variables and architecture
  operator   grade 13  Installs, configures and runs the product. Comfortable with a terminal.
             assumes a terminal, a package manager, environment variables, a hosting dashboard
             may not name internal symbols and architecture
  developer  grade 15  Builds against the product or contributes to it.
             assumes the language, the toolchain, and how to read source
             may name anything in the system

ISO/IEC/IEEE 26514 quality characteristics:
lines naming command-line flags: 1
--- user page ---
1 pages checked, 1 against a declared type, 0 stubs (frontmatter only)
no survey allowlist

DEFECTS (2)

  wrong-lens  (2)
      write it from the screen: what the reader sees, clicks, types and gets back
    guide.md:9  a 'user' page names a command-line flag, `--verbose`
    guide.md:9  a 'user' page names a command-line flag, `-v`
exit=1
--- operator page ---
1 pages checked, 1 against a declared type, 0 stubs (frontmatter only)
no survey allowlist
every page matches its declared type
exit=0
